<title>FRANCE: SGS-Thomson Q1 profit slips.</title>
<headline>SGS-Thomson Q1 profit slips.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-04-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Three months to March 29, 1997.</p>
<p>(Figures in millions of U.S. dollars unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net income				    90.5  vs	   175.0</p>
<p>    Earnings per share			  0.65  vs	    1.26</p>
<p>    Operating income			   113.5  vs	   220.7</p>
<p>    Pre-tax, pre-minority		    112.8  vs	   227.5</p>
<p>    Net interest expenses			0.7  vs	     0.5</p>
<p>    Net revenues				 944.9  vs	 1,027.7</p>
<p>    Net operating cash flow		   70.2  vs	    56.2</p>
<p>NOTE - SGS-Thomson said in a statement it expected its second quarter revenues to be around one billion dollars  </p>
<p>It said that the gross margin in the second half would be above the margin of the first half with sequential growth in the third and fourth quarters of 1997.</p>
<p>-- Paris newsroom +33 1 4221 5452</p>
</text>
